parse_json(json, on_error = None, max_nesting = -1, /)

Parse a JSON string to turn it into a Python object.

Parameters
----------
json : str
	A string in JSON syntax.
on_error : callable, optional
	Error handler. Will be invoked with the error code (see uni-json(3)) and
        error position in case of a parsing or resource usage related error. When
        not specified (None), a default handler raising a ValueError with a
        message containing the error code, the standard message associated with
        the error code and the position in the input string where the error occured
        will be called instead.
max_nesting : int, optional
	Maximum nested structure depth the parser is allowed to descent to. The parser
        will abort with an error if the maximum allowed nesting depth is exceeded. Defaults
        to -1 which means 'unlimited.

Returns
-------
object
	A Python object corresponding to the content of the string.

Raises
------
MemoryError
	A memory allocation failed during parsing.
ValueError
	A syntax error was encountered or the maximum structure
        nesting level was exceeded.
